#lang saffron
; The guard half of saffron-map-assoc-widens-value. A Saffron file may now
; assoc a float or a string into a `(Map Sym any)`, because the map's own type
; binds the value tyvar to `any`. That rule must key on what the CONTAINER is,
; not on the dialect: a map annotated `(Map Sym int)` in a Saffron file binds
; the same tyvar to `int`, so a float value is still a type error here.
;
; Without this fixture the widen could quietly relax into "a concrete argument
; at a tyvar parameter is always widened in a Saffron file", which would erase
; the element type of every annotated container in the dialect.

(defn main []
  (let [m  : (Map Sym int) (map-new)
        m2 (map-assoc m :a 7.25)]
    (println (map-get m2 :a)))
  0)
